From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:27:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: tests: probe errors, refused clocks, the
 last setup corners

The last error paths of the MT7986's bring-up that a test can reach:

mt7915_soc_test_probe_errors: a WMAC without an interrupt resource,
one whose interrupt can't be requested (IRQ_NOREQUEST), and one whose
SKU window can't be mapped: each probe stops with the device freed,
the last with its interrupt given back, nothing registered.
mt7915_soc_test_wmac_init_bad_clocks: mcu and ap2conn clocks whose
prepare fails are reported and the setup goes on.
mt7915_soc_test_sku_setup_error: A-die 0 read, A-die 1 not.
mt7915_soc_test_coninfra_setup: the MT7981's AP peripheral and efuse
bases.
mt7915_init_test_wiphy_wed: with a WED, the netdev offers TC offload.
mt7915 dma WED teardown: a second interface's WED is detached too.
mt76_eeprom_test_nvmem_read_error: an NVMEM provider that can't read
gives its error.

mt7915_soc_test_probe_remove calls the remove op through the driver's
pointer: called directly, the three-line function was inlined into
the test, where gcov didn't count it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
